1. What is the number of big coupons ? Anthony wants to send out twice as many big coupons as small coupons. He wants to send out 700 small coupons, so he wants to send out 2 * 700 = 1400 big coupons. 2. What is the cost of mailing small coupons ? Each small coupon costs 5 cents to mail. Anthony wants to send out 700 small coupons, so the cost of mailing small coupons is 700 * 5 = 3500 cents. 3. What is the cost of mailing big coupons ? Each big coupon costs 15 cents to mail. Anthony wants to send out 1400 big coupons, so the cost of mailing big coupons is 1400 * 15 = 21000 cents. 4. What is the total cost ? The total cost is the sum of the cost of mailing small coupons and the cost of mailing big coupons, which is 3500 + 21000 = 24500 cents. 5. Convert cents to dollars. Since 100 cents = 1 dollar, we divide the total cost in cents by 100 to get the total cost in dollars: 24500 / 100 = 245. 

So, Anthony spends 245 on postage total.

\boxed{245}
